==================================================================================================
0. do the artifacts agree with each other?
==================================================================================================
4 prediction files (A_plain, B_rot24, C_rotSO3, D_gravity_aligned) over 196733 test samples in 10 recordings; every sample answered once, and re-scoring each file from disk reproduces the accuracy and macro F1 in results_net.json to 1e-9
the setting the search runs with (D_gravity_aligned, per recording, score prob, margin 0.0) is one of the 64 scored on the validation users; the test users were scored once, after that choice
turned cases saved: 1: -y,x,z, 9: turned at random 3

==================================================================================================
1. the specification table (notebook cell 53), filled in from what was actually run
==================================================================================================
| network input (shape)  | (batch, 3, 256) - the three accelerometer axes in g at 50 Hz, 5.1 s per window; at evaluation every sample of a recording is answered once, from a full window, never from padding |
| network output (shape) | (batch, 7, 256) - seven logits per sample, one answer for every sample of the window, not one for the window |
| last layer             | nn.Conv1d(16, 7, 1), a 1 x 1 convolution; no softmax - softmax only for reading the probabilities, argmax for the answer |
| training loss          | CrossEntropyLoss(ignore_index=-1) over the 7 classes - the samples between activities (label -1) cost nothing, and a window in which EVERY sample is -1 is left out because torch returns NaN for it, not 0 |
| evaluation metric      | macro F1 over the 7 classes on the test users (mean of the per-class F1s, so the rare 3.6 s transition counts as much as standing), with accuracy alongside; -1 samples excluded |
| baseline               | always answering standing: test accuracy 0.176, macro F1 0.043 (the notebook says about 0.18 and 0.04); a second, stronger baseline answers one class per window by nearest class average (below) |
| network                | UNet(1, 3, 7, [16, 32, 64, 128]) from Part 1, 170k parameters, 400 epochs, batch 32, lr 0.001, Adam, best validation weights |

(paste-ready) network D_gravity_aligned is the arm the search was chosen on; the exported file is the same network without the search, since the app runs one forward pass per window

