==================================================================================================
6. what goes on the phone
==================================================================================================
the .onnx can only carry an arm that reads the raw axes the app feeds it: A_plain, B_rot24, C_rotSO3. D_gravity_aligned is the one the search was chosen on and it is NOT one of them - canonicalizing a window is work the app does not do.
export the best of those on validation - A_plain (0.942 validation macro F1) - with export_onnx.py: input acc 1 x 3 x 256, output logits 1 x 7 x 256, model_info with the class names, units g, 50 Hz, window 256, axes x,y,z. The app divides the browser's m/s2 by 9.80665 because the file says g.
the search is NOT in the .onnx either - the app does one forward pass per window - so what runs on the phone is one network with no second look. If the pocket is not the belt mount this data was collected with, the honest alternative is B_rot24, which is robust by training: 0.778 accuracy as it comes against 0.918 for A_plain, but 0.694 against 0.330 averaged over the turned wearings.
then on the phone: load the .onnx, Start, phone on the waist, and the script the notebook suggests - stand 20 s, walk 30 s, sit 20 s, take the stairs, lie down on a bench - Stop, and download the CSV.
